# fm84 in italiano.
#
# Each msgid is the English as the code has it, and the msgstr under it what
# is shown in its place. A sentence with a count in it has a msgstr for each
# form the count takes: [one] for 1, [other] for the rest. A msgctxt sets
# one use of a word apart from the same word elsewhere. {name} is a place
# the program fills, kept as it is. The letters to press - Y, N, A and the
# like - stay as they are; the names of the keys are written as an Italian
# keyboard has them: Maiusc, Invio, Canc, Spazio, PagSu/PagGiù.

